# Build output
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# A mis-parsed `dotnet` command on 23 Sep 2026 created a directory literally named
# "--nologo" and wrote 34 .wav files (69 MB) into it. Junk, not part of the port.
/--nologo/

# SIERRA'S DATA, NOT THIS PORT'S CODE.
#
# `assets/` is the extracted game — speech, art, fonts, raw resources — and `original/`
# is the shipped game itself. Neither is this project's work to redistribute, and
# together they are ~545 MB. Anyone building the port extracts their own copy from their
# own disks with tools/extract_resources.py and tools/extract_speech.py.
#
# `scripts/` IS tracked: it is the decompiled listing this port is written against, and
# every source file cites it by line. Remove it from the repository if that judgement
# turns out to be wrong.
/assets/
/original/

# Generated output, not source: frame strips and composed comparison images.
#
# The pattern is `/*` and not `/`, because git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded - a negation under `/tools/samples/` is silently ignored. Excluding
# the directory's CONTENTS instead leaves the directory itself tracked, so the negation
# below works.
/tools/samples/*

# CAST.md is the exception and it is not generated: it is the written record of what was
# measured while building the photoreal cast - every closed door, every instrument that
# failed and why, every number that argued against a change that was right. It was sitting
# in an ignored directory, so ~50 KB of two days' findings existed only on one disk and one
# `git clean` from gone.
!/tools/samples/CAST.md

# Candidate faces fetched for tools/make_font_sheets.py's comparison sheets. They are
# SAMPLES: no .csproj glob reaches tools/, nothing in src/ loads them, and the game's own
# bitmap fonts in assets/raw/font are still the only fonts it renders with. Ignored so a
# `git add -A` cannot quietly put a 2 MB TTF into the port.
/tools/fonts/

# The upscaler's native runtime (~79 MB of .dll/.dylib) — fetched, not authored.
/tools/Upscale/*
!/tools/Upscale/*.cs
!/tools/Upscale/*.csproj

# Build output: PublishJonesArt copies these out of assets/, which is itself ignored.
/src/Jones.App/Jones.App.Browser/wwwroot/art/

# The gh-pages worktree tools\deploy-web.ps1 stages the published site in. It is a
# checkout of the deployed branch, not source.
/.deploy/
# Build output: PublishJonesData copies these out of assets/, which is itself ignored.
/src/Jones.App/Jones.App.Browser/wwwroot/res/
